format session-log-v1
stamp 20260825.041416
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title A share needs a denominator -- the floor the card was dropping from the scan it cites
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Lap index from git log --oneline | wc -l = 3421 at the open, so the council rota reads row 3421 mod 5 = 1 -- Air and Saturn, law and boundary: TAME_CORE, single-stranded, and Gauge Style. The Saturn row governed directly. A bound is a law only where one number governs, and this lap found a number governing one reading and absent from the other that cites it.
think The roster stood green at 57 of 57 from this lap's own hot run, taken after git add on the tree the prior commit shipped, and the working tree is that commit with nothing modified. So the cold reading for this lap is that run rather than a fresh 25 minutes on an identical tree. No open agent-closable row stands in construction/REDS.md.
think Took the round my own recommend line named, and the measurement changed what the round was. I expected to invent a sentence floor for the report card's Register reading. prose_register_scan.sh already had one -- [ "$1" -ge 8 ] || continue, commented "too short to read a share from honestly" -- applied to its teaching tier and nowhere else.
think That reframes the whole thing. The card LIFTS measure() out of that scan precisely so the flip and the ceiling cannot disagree (REDS %201), and it was lifting the function while leaving the floor behind. So one page could be unmeasurable to the scan and scored 0 by the card, from the same awk.
think Measured before writing: 27 living teaching pages sit under the floor, and six read 100% from a SINGLE sentence -- docs-geode/libraries/README.md and docs-geode/press/README.md among them, both generated and both proven green by their own witness. On the door roster docs/README.md carries 2 sentences and foundations/README.md carries 7.
think Named the number as REGISTER_MIN_SENTENCES in prose_register_scan.sh, beside DOOR_MAX and FIELD_MAX where it belongs, and had the teaching loop use it. The card then reads it out with sed and refuses if it is absent, exactly as it already refuses when measure() goes missing. One floor, two readings, no way to drift.
think Chose ONE condition here rather than the two the index reading carries, and the difference is worth saying out loud: a page DECLARES itself an index, so that reading needs a second condition or the declaration is a door. A sentence count is MEASURED, so no page can assert its way under this floor.
think Left the 20% door wall untouched. The gate in prose_register_witness.rish reads 12 hand-chosen front doors with no floor, and adding one would create an exemption that changes nothing today and everything the first time a door reads high on two sentences. A gate that grows an exemption stops being a gate.
obs Then the control caught the trap before I shipped it. warm.md and cold.md, the two plants that prove the register reading discriminates, carry 6 and 5 sentences -- both UNDER the floor. Adding the floor without touching them would have made cold.md read 100 instead of 0, and cold_register_low would have gone from a real reading to a passing one that tests nothing.
obs Lengthened both past the floor. Then watched composite_is_mean fall from 100 to 98 and traced it to my own new sentence: "Each guard proves its refusal as well as its welcome" -- refusal is on the scan's own negative list. Rewrote it. Worth recording rather than quietly fixing: I wrote a negative word into the plant that exists to prove negative words are counted.
obs Planted the floor at its own boundary from both sides, which is the reading a single-sided plant cannot give. Seven refusal-led sentences read reported and cost nothing; the same prose with an eighth reads scored and reads low. So no page can sit AT the floor and be treated as if it were under it.
obs Nearly shipped an unmeasured number. I wrote "refuses 19 of 27" onto ITINERARY by adding this lap's 13 to the prior lap's 6, then ran the bite test and got 6 of 27 -- because HEAD already carries the prior round's readings, so that test measures only the floor batch. Corrected the card to what was actually measured against one named reference point.
obs The two crushed-index pages go F to A+ on their counted half, and README.md is untouched at 117 sentences scored. Door roster reads 12 of 12 at B or better with ceiling 0.
obs Left the design essay from the prior round alone. Its basename carries a one-clock stamp, which makes it testimony by the mark law, and it shipped an hour ago; the one-condition case lives in the witness header and in GAUGE_STYLE instead. Adding a section to shipped testimony to keep it current is what molt exists for, and this did not earn one.
obs The hot roster then reds nib_honesty, and it was right about me. I had written **Git nib:** `PENDING` as a placeholder, and that field is read BY NAME by a standing guard, so the card advertised a hash that resolves to nothing -- git_nib=absent, verdict=NO_NIB_FIELD. The seated pattern in remember-git-nib.md never wanted a placeholder: stage the card naming the CURRENT HEAD, commit, then amend once so the nib names the new one. Set it to 18b187b02a, guard GREEN, and re-ran the whole roster so the green measures the tree the commit ships rather than the tree before the repair.
obs Left it unbooked in construction/REDS.md on purpose, and the reason is the same one the exec-bit law gives: a guard catching a working-tree fault before the commit is the guard working, and the working tree is where repair costs one line. Nothing shipped wrong. Recording it here is the record it earns.
loom qa_register floor=8 living_pages_under=27 reading_100pct_off_one_sentence=6 door_pages_under=2
loom qa_card door_documents=12 below_b=0 ceiling=0 crushed_index_before=F crushed_index_after=A+
loom control behaviors=54 new_this_lap=10 old_card_refused=6 old_card_passed=4
file tools/fixtures/prose_register_scan.sh REGISTER_MIN_SENTENCES named beside DOOR_MAX; the teaching loop uses it rather than a literal
file tools/fixtures/qa_report_card.sh the floor cited from that scan, refusing when absent; register_mode reported below it
file tools/fixtures/qa_report_card_control.sh both plants lengthened past the floor; the boundary planted at 7 and at 8; the floor proven load-bearing
file tools/q/qa_report_card_witness.rish 10 asserts added, 54 behaviors, header names the third reading
file context/GAUGE_STYLE.md the Register row says floor and all; a third shape argued beside the other two
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now refilled; the bite figure corrected to what was measured; one lap row shelved
file construction/archive/20260825-003210_itinerary-landed-laps.md the shelved row
recommend keep-going the card is a document meter and says so nowhere -- pointed at qa_report_card_control.sh it reads F on 30 of 30 paths that are planted heredoc fixtures, and beside it Reach skips fenced code blocks where Truth does not (5 links, 4 unrostered files); decide between a --kind the card can be told and an honest refusal on a non-document, plant whichever from both sides, and stop the class at three
